<title>Developing an initial model to describe bacteria growth</title>

<p><ref>Video 1</ref> | <ref>Video 2 </ref> | <ref>Summary</ref> | <ref>Transcripts</ref> </p>


<description>
By analyzing some data and hypothesizing rules for cell division, we develop a discrete dynamical system for the growth of a population of bacteria.
</description>

<setup>
  <number name="B0" fixed="true">0.022</number>
  <number name="B1" fixed="true">0.036</number>
  <number name="B2" fixed="true">0.060</number>
  <number name="B3" fixed="true">0.101</number>
  <number name="B4" fixed="true">0.169</number>
  <number name="B5" fixed="true">0.266</number>
  <number name="dB1" fixed="true">$B1-$B0</number>
  <number name="dB2" fixed="true">$B2-$B1</number>
  <number name="dB3" fixed="true">$B3-$B2</number>
  <number name="dB4" fixed="true">$B4-$B3</number>
  <number name="dB5" fixed="true">$B5-$B4</number>
</setup>

