<setup>
  <math name="c">5/3</math>
  <math name="B32" simplify="numbers">$B0 $c^(32)</math>
</setup>
<exercise includeAutoNumber="true"><title />
<p>Using the equation described below and in the video, 
  <md name="specific_solution">
    <mrow>B_t &amp;= \bigg(\frac{5}{3}\bigg)^t B_0</mrow>
    <mrow>B_0 &amp;= 0.022</mrow>
  </md>
  where <m>t</m> is the number of time steps and <m>B_t</m> is the population at time step <m>t</m>, solve for <m>B_{32}</m>. Express your answer symbolically, or numerically to at least 2 decimal places.</p>
  <p><m>B_{32} = </m>
    <answer symbolicEquality="true" simplifyOnCompare="true" allowedErrorInNumbers="0.01" allowedErrorIsAbsolute="true" name="vid2Review1">
      <award>$B32</award>
    </answer>
  </p>

<hint hide="$vid2Review1.numSubmissions &lt; 2 or $vid2Review1.creditAchieved = 1 or $vid2Review1.numSubmissions >= 5">Use substitution for the variable <m>t</m> in the equation provided. The variable <m>t</m> represents the number of time steps under consideration.</hint>

<hint hide="$vid2Review1.numSubmissions &lt; 5 or $vid2Review1.creditAchieved = 1">Since we are considering the 32nd time step, we need to solve this equation for <m>t = 32</m>. We have,
  <md>
    <mrow>B_{32} \amp= <math extend="$B32" simplify="none" /></mrow>
    <mrow>\amp= $B32</mrow>
  </md>
</hint>
<solution>Since we are considering the 32nd time step, we need to solve this equation for <m>t = 32</m>. We have,
  <md>
    <mrow>B_{32} \amp= <math extend="$B32" simplify="none" /></mrow>
    <mrow>\amp= $B32</mrow>
  </md>
</solution>  
</exercise>

<exercise includeAutoNumber="true"><title />
<p>How many minutes have passed by time step <m>t = 32</m>? <answer name="vid2Review2">32*16</answer></p>

<hint hide="$vid2Review2.numSubmissions &lt; 2 or $vid2Review2.creditAchieved = 1 or $vid2Review2.numSubmissions >= 5">Recall that each time step corresponds to an interval of several minutes. See <ref to="$vid_section">Key Moment 1</ref> in the video for a clue.</hint>
</exercise>
<solution>Since there are 16 minutes between each time step, the total number of minutes is just <m>16 \cdot 32 = 512</m> minutes</solution>
</section>
 

